===================================================================
STEP 3: Iterative Mapping to Reduce Reference Bias
===================================================================
This approach:
1. Calls variants from initial Pachyramphus mapping
2. Creates Tityra pseudo-reference with variants incorporated
3. Remaps reads to Tityra pseudo-reference
4. Calls final high-confidence variants

This reduces reference bias with 2x computational cost vs 1000x for graphs

